Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Pin user-picked knowledge subjects into windows and the update

Reason: The desktop lets the user pick which knowledge subjects a video
belongs to, for reading and for write-back alike. Upstream reaches an entry
only when something asks for it -- a keyword in the user note, the
preparation task's judgment, or a window's `<requested_entries>` -- so a
picked subject could still be absent from every window. `knowledge_subjects=`
names the subjects task-statically, the same contract `--style` has:
`llm/knowledge/subjects.py` resolves them by qualified name (loudly on a
miss), renders their prompt projections as one budgeted block that rides next
to the style block in every correction window, and the post-task update pins
them at the head of each chunk's `<kb_entries>` so the model can propose into
them. Purely additive: without the argument every path is upstream's.

0.6.0 folded the correction into one value (`CorrectionRequest`) that every
front end fills, so the selection is a field there; `run_pipeline` keeps its
flat keyword and packs it like the other LLM keys. Injection follows
`knowledge_reads` (`read` and `update`), since `read` no longer collects
feedback but still reads the base; the update pin only matters under
`update`, which is the only mode that runs it. Entries are capped by their
category's own `max_entry_tokens`, as every other knowledge injection is now.

Removal: Delete once upstream accepts an explicit, task-static subject
selection for injection and knowledge write-back.

